            "title": "John K. Hunter, Notes on Partial Differential Equations, \u00a7\u00a72.7 and 3.7",
            "url": "https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/pdes/pde_notes.pdf"
          }
        ]
      },
      "statement": "Assume full AC. Fix $m\\ge1$, $2<q<4$, and $q^*=4q/(4-q)$. There are constants $\\delta=\\delta(m,q)>0$ and finite constants $K_2=K_2(m)$ and $K_q=K_q(m,q)$, having the following property. Let $B:\\mathbb R^4\\to\\operatorname{Hom}(\\mathbb R^{4m},\\mathbb R^m)$ be measurable, compactly supported and $\\|B\\|_4\\le\\delta$, where the pointwise norm is the operator norm. Let $f\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb R^m)\\cap L^q(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb R^m)$ be compactly supported. Set\n$$\\Phi(x)=\\frac{1}{4\\pi^2|x|^2},\\qquad Nv=\\Phi*v,\\qquad Hv=\\nabla Nv,$$\nwith the pole value chosen arbitrarily and all expressions interpreted as almost-everywhere classes. There is a unique $w\\in L^4(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb R^{4m})$ satisfying\n$$w=H(f+Bw).$$\nIt also belongs to $L^{q^*}$, satisfies $\\|w\\|_4\\le2K_2\\|f\\|_2$ and $\\|w\\|_{q^*}\\le2K_q\\|f\\|_q$, and is the gradient of\n$$u=N(f+Bw)\\in W^{2,q}_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb R^m),\\qquad -\\Delta u=f+B\\nabla u.$$\nThe fixed point is the limit of $w_0=0$, $w_{j+1}=H(f+Bw_j)$ in both indicated gradient norms.\n\nConsequently any compactly supported $v\\in W^{1,2}(\\mathbb R^4;\\mathbb R^m)$ with $\\nabla v\\in L^4$ satisfying $-\\Delta v=f+B\\nabla v$ distributionally equals this $u$ almost everywhere and belongs to $W^{2,q}_{\\mathrm{loc}}$. The smallness threshold is independent of the diameter of the supports: for the dilation $x=ry$, the transformed drift is $B_r(y)=rB(ry)$ and $\\|B_r\\|_4=\\|B\\|_4$.",
      "raw_sha256": "a737973e453510bec3baa267c6a326a431c3a084dea669beb3a8c2c1c98dfb7b",
      "dependency_level": "root recomputes"
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-critical-coulomb-transition-maps-have-holder-representatives",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "title": "Critical Coulomb transition maps have compatible Holder representatives",
      "deps": [
        "def-axiom-of-choice",
