        "lem-weak-leibniz-rule-with-a-smooth-factor",
        "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls",
        "thm-higher-order-sobolev-embedding",
        "thm-extension-theorem-for-bounded-smooth-domains"
      ],
      "proof_strategy": "direct",
      "provenance": {
        "statement": "literature-derived",
        "proof": "ai-altered"
      },
      "sources": {
        "references": [
          {
            "title": "Swarnendu Sil, Topology of weak G-bundles via Coulomb gauges in critical dimensions, Lemmas 11\u201312 and Theorem 16, pp.9\u201313",
            "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.07308"
          }
        ]
      },
      "statement": "Assume full AC. Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^4$ be open. Let $a,b\\in L^4_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega;\\mathfrak{su}(2)\\otimes\\mathbb R^4)$ satisfy $\\sum_i\\partial_i a_i=\\sum_i\\partial_i b_i=0$ distributionally. Suppose $h\\in W^{1,2}_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega;\\mathbb C^{2\\times2})$ takes values in $SU(2)$ almost everywhere and satisfies the transition equation\n$$\\partial_i h=hb_i-a_i h\\qquad(i=1,\\ldots,4)$$\ndistributionally. Then $h\\in W^{2,q}_{\\mathrm{loc}}(\\Omega)$ for every $2<q<4$ and has a unique continuous representative $h^*:\\Omega\\to SU(2)$, locally $C^{0,\\alpha}$ for every $0<\\alpha<1$.\n\nFor a finite open cover with given Coulomb forms $a_i$ and transition classes $h_{ij}$ satisfying these hypotheses on overlaps, any almost-everywhere identities $h_{ii}=1$, $h_{ji}=h_{ij}^{-1}$ and $h_{ij}h_{jk}=h_{ik}$ hold everywhere for the continuous representatives. Thus they form a continuous transition cocycle on the same open overlaps. Likewise any given almost-everywhere finite equivariance identities $h(\\gamma x)=\\rho(\\gamma)^{-1}h(x)\\rho(\\gamma)$, for $\\Gamma\\le O(4)$ preserving $\\Omega$ and a representation $\\rho:\\Gamma\\to SU(2)$, hold pointwise for $h^*$.\n\nThe regularity assertions are interior assertions on smaller balls compactly contained in $\\Omega$. No condition or regularity at $\\partial\\Omega$, no construction of a Coulomb gauge from curvature, and no existence of equivariant gauges is assumed or concluded.",
      "raw_sha256": "5c2d714bf662fa39e75bca1e74d37b1010a410fdaca4e7ddaad39861bcf5d36d",
      "dependency_level": "root recomputes"
    }
